### Product Management — IntelliJ HTTP Client requests
### Run these from IntelliJ (the gutter ▶ icon). Requires the app running on :8080.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Load the products table fragment (what the "Load products" button calls)
GET {{host}}/products
Accept: text/html

### 2. Add a new product (form-encoded, same payload the HTMX form sends)
POST {{host}}/products
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

title=HTTP Client Test Shorts&vendor=FAMME&productType=Shorts&variantTitle=Black / M&sku=TEST-BK-M&price=499.00&available=true

### 3. Add a product with no variant details (only the product row is created)
POST {{host}}/products
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

title=Minimal Product&vendor=ACME

### 4. The upstream source the scheduled job ingests (limited to 50 in the app)
GET https://famme.no/products.json?limit=250
Accept: application/json
